REFERENCE BASIS DATA / SOURCE NOTICES

Only O/H numeric records are shipped, not whole CamCASP basis files.
MAIN: Dunning, J. Chem. Phys. 90, 1007 (1989); Kendall, Dunning and
Harrison, J. Chem. Phys. 96, 6796 (1992). Original EMSL Basis Set Exchange.
Full expected contractions verified against MolSSI-BSE aug-cc-pVTZ v0;
ordered as CamCASP expected data. Native Psi4 O contractions omit terms
on separately present unit shells: same linear span, not literal equality.
RI AUX: Weigend, Koehn, Haettig, J. Chem. Phys. 116, 3175 (2002).
O/H numeric records and order verified against MolSSI-BSE aug-cc-pVTZ-RIFIT
v1 (2019-01-08; Turbomole 7.3). BSE spherical metadata is NOT adopted:
the traced protocol explicitly chooses Cartesian GAMINT.
BSE README explicitly releases its basis-set library under BSD-3-Clause:
https://github.com/MolSSI-BSE/basis_set_exchange (README.md, LICENSE).
BSE citation: Pritchard et al., J. Chem. Inf. Model. 59, 4814 (2019),
doi:10.1021/acs.jcim.9b00725. API/source hashes are pinned in the manifest.
No assumption is made that all CamCASP bundled data/components are MIT.

CamCASP permitted source-derived normalization/dispatch provenance:
Anthony Stone / Alston Misquitta. The applicable notice retained from the
owned CamCASP fixture is reproduced in full below. It is not a license
assertion about ORIENT, RRF, or third-party basis databases.

